  "evidence": "TEXT_D: +£2bn/year for education; class-size limits; building repairs; lifelong learning; Independent Bank of England; jobs/training and poverty‑trap reforms; 3,000 more police; faster justice and youth/restorative justice; housing expansion and rough‑sleeping target; NHS +£540m/year, shorter waits, recruit nurses/doctors, free eye/dental checks; tax/benefit changes to raise personal allowance and target high earners; environment/transport measures (public transport investment, carbon cuts); constitutional reform and devolution. TEXT_G: Single commitment to hold a referendum on Europe, offering a choice between a federal Europe and a looser trading association, with urgency and timing before/alongside the next general election; critiques main parties’ euro‑only referendum offers.",
